## OAI/OpenAPI-Specification — `webhook-example.json`

`src/root.zig`'s test `"conformance: the checker accepts the OpenAPI
Initiative's own published v3.1 example"` embeds (`oai_webhook_example`) a
verbatim copy of `examples/v3.1/webhook-example.json` from
https://github.com/OAI/OpenAPI-Specification, pinned at the `3.1.0` tag
(commit path `examples/v3.1/webhook-example.json`, fetched 2026-08-01). The
repository is licensed Apache License 2.0 (its `LICENSE` file), copyright the
OpenAPI Initiative.

Purpose: this document is used purely as a frozen, offline ANCHOR for a
hand-written OpenAPI 3.1 structural validator (`validateOpenApi31`) —
proving the checker accepts a real, externally-authored conformant document
(one that deliberately omits `paths` in favor of `webhooks`/`components`, a
shape this module's own generator never produces), not merely this module's
own output shape. No OpenAPI Initiative source code of any kind is used,
ported, or consulted — only this one example JSON document.
